#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096406 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Two Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "28008aa6-6be6-52dd-9459-097113538b13" :question/math-academy-id "e-501" :question/problem "Express $\\dfrac{2x-1}{(x+2)(x-3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x-1}{(x+2)(x-3)} = \\dfrac{A}{(x+2)} +\\dfrac{B}{(x-3)}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above expression through by $(x+2)(x-3)$ gives\n\n$$\n2x-1= A(x-3)+B(x+2)\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2$ gets rid of the $B$ term and allows us to solve for $A$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(-2) - 1 &= A(-2 - 3) + B(-2 + 2) \\\\\n- 5 &= A(-5) + B(0) \\\\\nA &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=3$ gets rid of the $A$ term and allows us to solve for $B$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(3) - 1 &= A(3 - 3) + B(3 + 2) \\\\\n5 &= A(0) + B(5) \\\\\nB &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKnowing that $A=1$ and $B=1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x-1}{(x+2)(x-3)} = \\dfrac{1}{(x+2)} +\\dfrac{1}{(x-3)}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096410 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e66d7cf-1a4b-51e6-9c78-f70a8c0555df" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Three Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "d10d11a8-6a30-59b6-bb0e-6065e60bbc6b" :question/math-academy-id "e-502" :question/problem "Express $\\dfrac{2x^2+5x+7}{(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$, $B$, and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^2+5x+7}{(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)} = \\dfrac{A}{x+2} + \\dfrac{B}{x-3} + \\dfrac{C}{x+1}\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply both sides of the equation by $(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)$ to clear the fractions:\n\n$$\n2x^2+5x+7= A(x-3)(x+1)+B(x+2)(x+1)+C(x+2)(x-3)\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2$ gets rid of the $B$ and $C$ terms and allows us to solve for $A$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(-2)^{2} + 5(-2) + 7 &= A(-2 - 3)(-2 + 1) \\\\\n5 &= A(5) \\\\\nA &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=3$ gets rid of the $A$ and $C$ terms and allows us to solve for $B$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(3)^{2} + 5(3) + 7 &= B(3 + 2)(3 + 1) \\\\\n40 &= B(20) \\\\\nB &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, plugging in $x=-1$ gets rid of the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(-1)^{2} + 5(-1) + 7 &= C(-1 + 2)(-1 - 3) \\\\\n4 &= C(-4) \\\\\nC &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKnowing that $A=1$, $B=2$, and $C=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^2+5x+7}{(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)} = \\dfrac{1}{x+2} +\\dfrac{2}{x-3} -\\dfrac{1}{x+1}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289074 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Two Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77fa05a0-065f-55e0-8772-10a5bc27239c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289076} {:answer/id #uuid "6a91d886-93d0-55d4-8332-e22191fabdbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289077} {:answer/id #uuid "20089555-b2b4-5881-a546-c245548b5d8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289078} {:answer/id #uuid "c1f0d6d2-2f1c-5b64-ac9e-f8c29191a81e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289079} {:answer/id #uuid "74990dcd-b63e-5bb8-9b9e-0d439fcabe1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1f0d6d2-2f1c-5b64-ac9e-f8c29191a81e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289079} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cbf946a-6bde-519f-b590-8ddb36f996c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289075}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "49eb189d-dbb6-571c-b92b-059f64da6668" :question/math-academy-id "q-10972" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{6x-25}{x(x+5)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{(x+5)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, calculate $A+B.$" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6x-25}{x(x+5)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{(x+5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $x(x+5)$ gives\n\n$$\n6x-25=A(x+5)+B(x).\n$$\n\nFor $x=0$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(0)-25 & =A(0+5)+B(0) \\\\ -25 & =5A \\\\ A & =-\\frac{25}{5} \\\\ A & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(-5)-25 & =A(-5+5)+B(-5) \\\\ -55 & =-5B \\\\ B & =\\frac{-55}{-5} \\\\ B & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA+B=-5+11=6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Two Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98c323c9-b4b7-55de-b8fb-b1fc59ed12ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255561} {:answer/id #uuid "3d30d3f4-7110-5d7a-94f1-05de257882c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255562} {:answer/id #uuid "db33c0c3-efd2-5101-8afc-0e00d60594ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255563} {:answer/id #uuid "3e25788b-7544-5f2b-9242-937076aff43b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255564} {:answer/id #uuid "c348aa84-f04d-5685-8e7d-055cf33fe3ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98c323c9-b4b7-55de-b8fb-b1fc59ed12ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255561} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc4fc8d6-5aac-5a3d-a9b2-82befae980c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ca8ed292-7934-54b0-b0fb-7d888622b0ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-10974" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7x-37}{(5-3x)(2x+3)}=\\frac{A}{(5-3x)}+\\frac{B}{(2x+3)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, calculate $A+B.$" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x-37}{(5-3x)(2x+3)}=\\frac{A}{(5-3x)}+\\frac{B}{(2x+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(5-3x)(2x+3)$ gives\n\n$$\n7x-37=A(2x+3)+B(5-3x).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{3}{2}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(-\\frac{3}{2})-37 & =A(2(-\\frac{3}{2})+3)+B(5-3(-\\frac{3}{2})) \\\\ \\frac{-21-74}{2} & =B(\\frac{10+9}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{-95}{2} & =B(\\frac{19}{2}) \\\\ B & =\\frac{-95}{19} \\\\ B & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=\\frac{5}{3}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(\\frac{5}{3})-37 & =A(2(\\frac{5}{3})+3)+B(5-3(\\frac{5}{3})) \\\\ \\frac{35-111}{3} & =A(\\frac{10+9}{3}) \\\\ A & =\\frac{-76}{19} \\\\ A & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA+B=-4+(-5)=-4-5=-9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096864 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e66d7cf-1a4b-51e6-9c78-f70a8c0555df" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Three Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be68e142-9d17-56e3-848c-1b72b082a31c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6)/((2x + 1)) + (2)/((x + 5)) - (11)/((x + 1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093592} {:answer/id #uuid "1f757042-e4a1-554d-b16d-4da22ea8f9d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1)/((2x + 1)) + (3)/((x + 5)) - (2)/((x + 1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093593} {:answer/id #uuid "345ef20a-3f1b-5298-9488-3f854c9abd66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (2)/((2x + 1)) + (4)/((x + 5)) + (5)/((x + 1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093594} {:answer/id #uuid "4b402463-0065-51ea-8fca-7d152a65bf58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (1)/((2x + 1)) + (6)/((x + 5)) - (3)/((x + 1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093595} {:answer/id #uuid "53acb89b-cf3f-53bc-8174-ab692ea114e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (4)/((2x + 1)) + (7)/((x + 5)) + (4)/((x + 1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "345ef20a-3f1b-5298-9488-3f854c9abd66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (2)/((2x + 1)) + (4)/((x + 5)) + (5)/((x + 1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093594} :answer-field/id #uuid "589432c7-1073-5e41-9823-b0fe65045453" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093591}] :question/id #uuid "c52ae0a6-ddb7-585f-9b74-6be345d63c9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-10981" :question/problem "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nExpress $(16x^{2} + 55x + 19)/((2x + 1)(x + 5)(x + 1))$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e66d7cf-1a4b-51e6-9c78-f70a8c0555df" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Three Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c326bf8e-2b8b-5dd6-b7d2-52577291f94c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4)/((x + 1)) - (6)/((2 - x)) - (7)/((x + 3))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093598} {:answer/id #uuid "d264dacd-baf6-5b64-99d4-570051c1e39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3)/((x + 1)) + (5)/((2 - x)) + (4)/((x + 3))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093599} {:answer/id #uuid "e289503f-8c52-5b9f-acec-676b54e03fae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8)/((x + 1)) + (1)/((2 - x)) + (2)/((x + 3))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093600} {:answer/id #uuid "61c5bf61-37b5-542a-92f5-fc05b1823fca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3)/((x + 1)) - (2)/((2 - x)) + (6)/((x + 3))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093601} {:answer/id #uuid "71d5bdac-5ec1-5d38-8f77-e8b38ecb7437" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2)/((x + 1)) - (1)/((2 - x)) - (3)/((x + 3))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093602}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d264dacd-baf6-5b64-99d4-570051c1e39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3)/((x + 1)) + (5)/((2 - x)) + (4)/((x + 3))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093599} :answer-field/id #uuid "52353003-cdba-5f9b-aa22-71bc1949607f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093597}] :question/id #uuid "ea90bdf7-7ef9-5956-892d-81c701801ca4" :question/math-academy-id "q-10989" :question/problem "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nExpress $(-2x^{2} + 21x + 41)/((x + 1)(2 - x)(x + 3))$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289089 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Two Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df797e27-a173-5b04-9f46-8d090078f38e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df797e27-a173-5b04-9f46-8d090078f38e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289091} :answer-field/id #uuid "92430816-e191-55f5-a35c-fd2663b67f23" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fbf7949e-794d-58c7-ac2f-19452bc80c32" :question/math-academy-id "q-350930" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{3x+5}{(x-3)(2x+1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n|  | $\\frac{3x+5}{(x-3)(2x+1)}\\,=\\,\\frac{2}{x-3}\\,\\,+$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $2x+1$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+5}{(x-3)(2x+1)}=\\frac{2}{x-3}+\\frac{B}{2x+1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-3)(2x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n3x+5=2(2x+1)+B(x-3).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-\\frac{1}{2})+5 & =2(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)+B(-\\frac{1}{2}-3) \\\\ \\frac{7}{2} & =-\\frac{7}{2}B \\\\ B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+5}{(x-3)(2x+1)}=\\frac{2}{x-3}+\\frac{-1}{2x+1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268292 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e66d7cf-1a4b-51e6-9c78-f70a8c0555df" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Three Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b30ba91-ae46-5c8a-a706-eadf49473929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{(x-3)}+\\frac{3}{(x-1)}+\\frac{2}{(x+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268294} {:answer/id #uuid "5487de66-7dc7-5034-8054-c95e685f72e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{(x-3)}+\\frac{4}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268295} {:answer/id #uuid "caf3373e-14ce-53af-958f-71db5e3cd93e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{(x-3)}-\\frac{2}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268296} {:answer/id #uuid "b551016b-e3f4-554b-afb5-1871fb7b2e49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(x-3)}+\\frac{2}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268297} {:answer/id #uuid "39114682-6ec7-594e-8ef7-e381555c6285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(x-3)}-\\frac{2}{(x-1)}+\\frac{2}{(x+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caf3373e-14ce-53af-958f-71db5e3cd93e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{(x-3)}-\\frac{2}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268296} :answer-field/id #uuid "22269ea3-ba61-5af1-b9c9-78ad9e0d52ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e23b9540-6b27-5f85-a262-32ee244fff8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-69751" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{12x+12}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12x+12}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)} & =\\frac{A}{(x-3)}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)}+\\frac{C}{(x+5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)$ gives\n\n$$\n12x+12=A(x-1)(x+5)+B(x-3)(x+5)+C(x-3)(x-1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=3$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(3)+12 & =A(3-1)(3+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(3-3)(3+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(3-3)(3-1) \\\\ 36+12 & =A(2)(8) \\\\ A & =\\frac{48}{16} \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(1)+12 & =A(1-1)(1+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(1-3)(1+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(1-3)(1-1) \\\\ 12+12 & =B(-2)(6) \\\\ B & =\\frac{24}{-12} \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(-5)+12 & =A(-5-1)(-5+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(-5-3)(-5+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(-5-3)(-5-1) \\\\ -60+12 & =C(-8)(-6) \\\\ C & =\\frac{-48}{48} \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{12x+12}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)}=\\frac{3}{(x-3)}-\\frac{2}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}.\n$$"}]}
